# Git & deployment

## Branching
- ALWAYS create a working branch first: `git checkout -b <name>`. NEVER edit on `master`.
- Parallel Claude/Cursor sessions run on this repo — branch isolation prevents commits from sweeping each other's unstaged files.
- No `--no-verify`, no force-push to `master`, no amending published commits.

## CI gate (before any PR)
- `bun run ci` — full lint + type-check + unit + migration-naming check.
- Failures block deploy; investigate and fix the root cause, never bypass.

## Deploy
- Production: `bash scripts/deploy.sh` (deploys to `app.isaflow.co.za`).
- The deploy script enforces lint ratchet baselines and the migration-naming gate.
- Production deploys are blocked during business hours (08:00–17:00 SAST, Mon–Fri) without explicit approval.

## Migrations
- New SQL goes in `scripts/migrations/sql/` with the next unused 3-digit prefix.
- Never reuse a prefix. Use `244b_` style suffix to insert between existing numbers.
- `IF NOT EXISTS` on all `CREATE TABLE` / `CREATE INDEX`.
